Added a "Fields to Export" picker to the export dialog and to the `Export Object List` Job's own form, for checking the specific fields to export - including fields of related objects, such as a device's manufacturer, and each custom field - and dragging them into the order the columns should appear in.
Added a "Match the list view" button to that picker, which fills the selection in with the columns the list view is displaying, in the order it displays them - those of the saved view in use, else your own table configuration, else the table's defaults - so they can be reviewed and adjusted before the export runs. A related-object-count column is carried across as the relation it counts, where an export can emit that relation; any column with no exportable equivalent is named rather than quietly dropped.
Added a download button to the export progress dialog, offering the exported file as soon as the export finishes.
Added support for a Job variable's form field to be configured from the rest of the Job form, through a `configure_for_form()` method, so that an App can offer a variable whose choices depend on what another variable is set to.
